WEBVTT

00:00:04.101 --> 00:00:17.435
Typecase comes as a Flatpak, a kind of app that runs on almost every Linux. On Ubuntu, Flatpak needs a short setup, just once. On Fedora or Linux Mint it's already there, so you can skip this video.

00:00:17.736 --> 00:00:26.015
Everything happens in the Terminal. Open it from the search, or press Control, Alt and T. Don't worry: three commands, and you're done.

00:00:26.783 --> 00:00:38.305
First, install Flatpak itself. Ubuntu asks for your password: type it, the letters stay invisible, and press Enter. When Ubuntu asks whether to continue, press Enter again.

00:00:38.618 --> 00:00:44.956
Second, teach the Software app about Flatpak. That's what lets you install Typecase with a double click.

00:00:48.259 --> 00:00:52.420
Third, add Flathub. Typecase gets the parts it needs from there.

00:00:55.643 --> 00:01:02.535
That's it. Restart your computer once, so that new apps show up. You'll find the commands below this video, ready to copy.

00:01:03.435 --> 00:01:06.167
Typecase. Free software, made for GNOME.

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:09.050
With love, by kleinod.studio.
